# GLOBAL PROJECT INSTRUCTIONS

You are acting as a senior full-stack software engineer, SaaS product architect, UI/UX designer and QA engineer.

Build a complete, functional, responsive project management SaaS application named **TeamFlow**.

This is a serious portfolio project intended to demonstrate professional full-stack development skills. Do not create a basic college CRUD application.

## Product vision

TeamFlow allows organizations to:
- Create and manage workspaces.
- Invite team members.
- Organize projects.
- Assign tasks and subtasks.
- Track progress using Kanban boards.
- Collaborate through comments and real-time updates.
- Monitor deadlines.
- Analyze team productivity.
- Manage files and notifications.

## Mandatory development rules

1. Inspect the existing repository before creating or modifying files.
2. Preserve existing working code unless there is a documented reason to change it.
3. Use the specified technology stack throughout the application.
4. Never create fake functionality or buttons that do nothing.
5. Every form must have validation, loading, success and error states.
6. All important data must persist in MongoDB.
7. Never use hardcoded dashboard statistics when real database data is available.
8. Never expose secrets, passwords or JWT tokens in frontend source code or logs.
9. Implement proper backend authorization. Hiding buttons in React is not security.
10. Use reusable components and maintain clean separation of concerns.
11. Avoid unnecessarily complicated abstractions.
12. Use realistic seed data only for development and demos.
13. Do not silently ignore errors.
14. Do not claim a feature is complete until it has been implemented and tested.
15. Run the relevant tests after each major implementation.
16. Keep dependencies compatible with the actual installed Node.js and package versions.
17. Never overwrite .env files containing user secrets. Provide .env.example instead.
18. Do not proceed past a stage with unresolved critical errors.

